---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import company from '../data/company.json';
const toc = [
  { id: 'who', label: 'Who we are' },
  { id: 'what', label: 'What we collect' },
  { id: 'why', label: 'Why we use it' },
  { id: 'who-sees', label: 'Who processes it' },
  { id: 'how-long', label: 'How long we keep it' },
  { id: 'rights', label: 'Your rights' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes' },
];
---
<Legal title="Privacy policy" description="How Reef Support B.V. collects, uses and protects personal data sent through reef.support, and how to exercise your rights under the GDPR." updated="19 November 2026" toc={toc}>
  <h2 id="who">Who we are</h2>
  <p>This website is run by {company.legalName}, registered with the Netherlands Chamber of Commerce (KvK) under number {company.kvk}, {company.registeredAddress}. We are the controller for personal data sent to us through this website. You can reach us at <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="what">What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Contact form:</strong> your name, organisation, email address and message, plus the country, ecosystem and reason for contact if you give them.</li>
    <li><strong>Field notes sign-up:</strong> your email address.</li>
    <li><strong>Server logs:</strong> our hosting provider records technical data such as IP address, browser type and the pages requested, to keep the site secure and working.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not use analytics, advertising trackers or cookies, and we do not build profiles of visitors.</p>

  <h2 id="why">Why we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Contact form details are used only to reply to you and to follow up on your request. The legal basis is your consent, given with the checkbox on the form.</li>
    <li>Sign-up addresses are used only to send field notes, about once a month. The legal basis is your consent; every email lets you unsubscribe.</li>
    <li>Server logs are kept for security and to keep the site running. The legal basis is our legitimate interest in a safe, working website.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="who-sees">Who processes it</h2>
  <p>We do not sell or share your data. We use two service providers that process data on our behalf:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Vercel Inc.</strong> hosts this website and keeps short-lived server logs.</li>
    <li><strong>FormSubmit</strong> (formsubmit.co) delivers contact form messages and sign-ups to our inbox by email.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Both providers may process data outside the European Economic Area. Where they do, the transfer relies on safeguards recognised under the GDPR, such as the EU Standard Contractual Clauses. Fonts and all other site files are served from our own domain, so no other third party receives your data when you visit.</p>

  <h2 id="how-long">How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Contact messages: up to 24 months after our last exchange, unless they lead to a contract, in which case we keep them as long as the law requires.</li>
    <li>Sign-up addresses: until you unsubscribe or ask us to remove them.</li>
    <li>Server logs: kept by the host for a short period, typically no more than 30 days.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask us to see, correct, delete or export the personal data we hold about you, to restrict or object to its use, and to withdraw your consent at any time. Email <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a> and we will respond within one month. If you are not satisfied with our answer, you can complain to the Dutch Data Protection Authority (Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens).</p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy when the website or the services we use change. The date at the top of this page shows the latest version.</p>
</Legal>
